  "text": "Welcome back to the workshop where return raw footage into finished films. Today I will show you three simple tricks that save about two hours of editing time. First, always cut on the beat, because rhythm is what keeps the audience awake. Second, remove the silent gaps longer than half a second before you touch the colors. Third, normalize the audio to minus sixty sixteen l u fs, which is the standard for online video platforms. Finally, export at fifteen megabits per second, and never trust the first render. That is it for this episode see you in the next one.",
